# --- .NET ---
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/
artifacts/
*.user
.vs/
TestResults/
*.trx
*.coverage

# The config file holds the static tokens and the SSH credentials, and
# docs/DESIGN.md §6.1 requires it to be mode 0600 on disk. A copy of it in git is
# the same secret with the file mode removed, so the pattern is here rather than
# in a reviewer's head. `sshwarden.example.toml` is checked in on purpose and is
# excluded below - it carries placeholder values that the loader refuses.
sshwarden.toml
*.sshwarden.toml
!sshwarden.example.toml

# SSH private keys, whatever they get named locally.
*.pem
*.key
id_ed25519*
id_rsa*

# The audit log is the deployment's record of what ran on its own production
# hosts, including command output. It is the one artefact of this project that
# must never leave the machine that produced it.
*.jsonl
audit/

# A brief written to an agent rather than to a reader of this project. Nothing of the kind is
# checked in and nothing here needs one - the design this repository was built from is
# docs/DESIGN.md, in English, carrying the section numbers the code cites. The rule stays because
# a note like that is written for one deployment and reads like documentation to everyone else,
# and this is the cheapest place to stop one being committed by accident.
HANDOFF.md
